WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.620
For administrators, Privileged Identity

2
00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.850
Management turns privilege
into a governed request.

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.800
An administrator holds an eligible
assignment, not an active one.

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.315
To use it, they ask for activation
with a reason and a ticket,

5
00:00:13.315 --> 00:00:16.464
step up their sign-in, get
approval from someone else,

6
00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:20.638
and receive a time-boxed activation
that's logged and later reviewed.

7
00:00:20.638 --> 00:00:24.037
The details matter, and the
old guides had several wrong.

8
00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:26.951
Activation runs from one
to twenty-four hours.

9
00:00:26.951 --> 00:00:30.643
PIM's built-in MFA can be
satisfied by an earlier sign-in,

10
00:00:30.643 --> 00:00:35.075
so the book forces a fresh step-up
with an authentication context.

11
00:00:35.075 --> 00:00:37.650
Approvers can't approve
their own requests.

12
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:41.800
And if the PIM licenses lapse,
eligible assignments are removed.

13
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:47.370
Appendix B sets each role's activation
time, approvers and notifications,

14
00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:51.460
tighter for Tier 0 and Tier
1 than Book 02's first table.
